special_abilities:
  - name: "Special R.C.C. Abilities Common to Lemurians"
    description: "A Lemurian Guardsman keeps every racial ability of the Lemurian R.C.C. (printed 50-51): Life Sense at a 25 foot (7.6 m) radius plus 5 feet (1.5 m) per level, 20% +5% per level to locate a specific kind of animal or plant and +5% more underwater; Empathy with Animals other than monsters, predators and sentient creatures; Ley Line Powers (heals and recovers P.P.E. twice as fast as a human on a ley line or at a stone pyramid, and swims 25% faster along a ley line); the Lemurian Natural Abilities; and Ultrasonic Communication out to 2,000 feet (610 m) underwater or 400 feet (122 m) in air. A Guardsman is likely to keep an Aquatic Lemur as a pet or Familiar. These belong to the Lemurian race, not to the occupation: a Meran or Ichthylean Guardsman has his own race''s abilities instead."
  - name: "Trained in Combat and Rescue"
    description: "Guardsman training covers weapons and fighting and, equally, rescue work and giving aid in any kind of emergency. It grants no number of its own; the O.C.C. skill list is where it shows."
  - name: "Guardsman Psionics"
    description: "A Major Psychic with a fixed set of eight powers: Death Trance, Empathy, Intuitive Combat, Mind Block, See the Invisible, Stop Bleeding, Suppress Fear and Telepathy. I.S.P. is 1D6x10 plus the M.E. attribute number, +2D4 per level of experience. No other psionic powers are available to the character, at creation or later; these replace the standard Lemurian psionics."
  - name: "Perception: Plants and Nature"
    description: "The +2 on Perception Rolls applies in general and also to rolls involving plants and nature. The general +2 is in the stored bonuses; nothing extra is added for plants and nature."
  - name: "Lemurian War Steed"
    description: "Every Guardsman has one specific Lemurian War Steed assigned to him (player''s choice of steed), and may be given the use of others for an assignment. The steed is a creature, not an item, so it is not in the equipment list; the Living Saddle and Morphic Riding Bio-Barding issued with it are."
  - name: "Pay and Quarters"
    description: "Monthly salary of 2,100 credits or the same in trade goods, doubled for Royal Guardsmen and top officers; the character starts with one month''s pay. Even a low-ranking Guardsman usually has a family estate in one of the floating cities, and there are barracks for long duty: each houses four Guardsmen and has a lavatory, sitting room, study and small kitchen."
  - name: "Issued Gear and Bio-Skins"
    description: "Special or additional weapons and gear may be assigned for particular situations and missions, and the Guardsman has access to every type of Bio-Skin. The Bio-Armor chosen tends to match temperament and posting: Chitin, Coral and Crustacean for defensive positions, guard duty and front-line combat; Kelp for stealth, reconnaissance and scouting; Dolphin for patrols and quick response; Shark for special operations and all kinds of combat. Clothing is organically grown and woven - uniforms, formal wear and combat clothes, most of it suited to use underwater - along with other common personal items."
restrictions:
  - "Alignment: any. Most are Principled (40%), Scrupulous (35%), Unprincipled (15%) or Aberrant (3%, the honorable kind)."
  - "Attribute requirements: P.S. 14 and P.E. 11 or higher. Other high physical attributes and a high I.Q. are suggested but not required."
  - "Race: Lemurians (85%), Merans (8%), Ichthyleans (6%) and assorted other species (1%) have become Oceanic Guardsmen."
  - "Psionics: the eight Guardsman powers only. No other psionics are available to this character."
  - "Cybernetics: none. Lemurians have no interest in bionics, not even Bio-Systems."
  - "Pilot: Jet Packs means Lemurian Squid Packs, and Jet Aircraft and Submersibles mean Lemurian craft only. Boats are sail or paddle types only."
extraction_notes: |
  - Lemuria, printed 68-70 (the description on 68, the abilities, bonuses and
    the head of the stat block on 69, the rest of the skills, the equipment
    and the money on 70), under the section heading "Lemurian Men-At-Arms
    O.C.C.s"; hence `men_of_arms: true` and `occ_group: men-of-arms`. The class
    states no `sdc_base`; +3D6 S.D.C. (printed 69) is a pool bonus.
  - XP LADDER: printed 86, the column headed "Oceanic Guardsman & Ichthyleans",
    read off a render of the page (the text layer is damaged there). The
    stored figures are the lower bound of each level.
  - SKILLS KNOWN BY ALL LEMURIANS ARE PRINTED ON THIS CLASS''S PAGE WITH THIS
    CLASS''S FIGURES. Printed 69: Language: Lemurian and Oceanic at 96%;
    Literacy: Lemurian at 85% +1% per level; Mathematics: Basic at 82 +1% per
    level; Swimming at 80% +2% per level. The Lemurian R.C.C. on printed 50
    prints Swimming at 78% +2%, so the block is not a plain copy of the race''s.
    Stored on this class: Language: Oceanic 96 and Swimming 80 +2, because the
    O.C.C. Skills list does not otherwise grant either. NOT stored from that
    block: Language: Lemurian 96 (the O.C.C. Skills list prints 98),
    Literacy: Lemurian 85 (see the next note; its +1% per level IS the rate stored) and Mathematics: Basic 82 +1
    (the O.C.C. Skills list prints +20%, stored as 65 +5). A non-Lemurian
    Guardsman is therefore handed Oceanic and Swimming that the book gives to
    Lemurians only.
  - LITERACY: LEMURIAN IS PRINTED THREE WAYS ON ONE PAGE. Printed 69 has "Language and Literacy: Lemurian (Native)
    at 98%", then "Literacy: Lemurian at 96%" (top of printed 70), and the
    all-Lemurians block has 85% +1% per level. Granted by name as
    `Literacy: Lemurian` at 96, taken from the stand-alone literacy line
    rather than the combined language-and-literacy one. No per-level figure
    is printed for the 98% or 96% lines; the +1% of the all-Lemurians line
    is stored.
  - NO PER-LEVEL FIGURE IS PRINTED for Language: Lemurian (98%) or Language:
    Oceanic (96%); 1 is stored for both, the native-speaker rate the skill
    descriptions print on printed 55.
  - W.P. ANCIENT: TWO and W.P. MODERN: TWO are each stored as two picks from
    the whole Weapon Proficiencies category. The catalog does not split that
    category into ancient and modern, so the split is in the notes only.
  - HAND TO HAND: KAPU KUIALUA is the catalog''s `Hand to Hand: Demon Combat`
    (printed 54-57 use both names), priced as `demon_combat: 2`.
  - RELATED SKILLS (printed 70). "Aquatic: Any (+10%)" is one entry named Aquatic whose
    only list names the book''s Aquatic Skills (printed 54) at +10%, since there is no Aquatic
    category in the catalog; it leaves out the four this class grants as O.C.C. skills,
    Sea Holistic Medicine (printed under Medical at +5%) and Horsemanship: Serpent Hunter.
    Creative Writing and the languages are Technical
    rows, where the class''s Technical: Any (+5%) already reaches them at the
    same +5%. The Communications entry names the catalog''s own Communications
    rows for Language and Literacy and leaves out `Language: All (magical)`
    and the already granted `Literacy: Lemurian`. "(Sea) Holistic Medicine" is stored as `Sea Holistic Medicine`
    only, not also `Holistic Medicine`. "Submersibles (Lemurian only)" is
    stored as `Boat: Submersibles`, not `Military: Submersibles`. "Military
    Fortifications" is the catalog''s `Military Fortification`; "Programming"
    is `Computer Programming`; "Jet Pack" is `Jet Packs`. Cowboy, Electrical
    and Mechanical are None and are simply not listed.
  - PSIONICS (printed 69). The book prints an I.S.P. cost beside each power: Death Trance
    (2), Empathy (4), Intuitive Combat (10), Mind Block (4), See the Invisible
    (4), Stop Bleeding (4), Suppress Fear (4), Telepathy (4). The catalog holds
    Death Trance at 1, Stop Bleeding at 2 and Suppress Fear at 8; the catalog
    rows are left alone and the book''s figures are recorded here. "See the
    Invisible" is the catalog''s `See The Invisible`.
  - BONUSES (printed 69). Stored: +2 P.S., +1 P.P., +3D6 S.D.C., +2 Perception, +1 attack
    per melee round, +2 pull punch, +1 vs possession, +1 vs mind control, and
    +1 vs Horror Factor at levels 2, 4, 6, 8, 10, 12 and 14. "+2 on Perception
    Rolls in general and involving plants and nature" is stored as one +2.
  - EQUIPMENT (printed 70). The Bio-Armor line lists six armors to select from (Chitin,
    Coral, Dolphin, Kelp, Wood, Shark) and then, in the next sentence, calls
    Crustacean Bio-Armor typical for defensive postings. Crustacean is NOT in
    the select list and is not offered. The three symbiotes of choice are
    offered from the eight symbiote rows of the Bio-Construct Symbiotes
    section, printed 136 onward (the four
    Bio-Skins are left out, since the class has access to all of them anyway)
    plus three weapons read as non-lethal; the book does not name the
    non-lethal weapons. The melee choice is every melee Bio-Weapon row, the Serpent
    Entangler Net included, less the two Serpent Bio-Weapons, which their
    catalog rows describe as reserved for Serpent Hunters. The
    long-range choice is every row of the Lemurian Ranged Weapons section
    other than the Stonecaster Pistol already issued. "Organically grown and
    woven clothes (uniforms, dress/formal wear, and combat clothes)" is stored
    as the generic uniform, dress uniform and clothing rows. The War Steed is
    a creature and is prose.
  - MONEY. One month''s pay, 2,100 credits or trade goods (printed 70, right
    column). The Money paragraph on printed 68 (2,000 credits, squadron
    leaders, barracks for three) is the END OF THE BIRDMAN WARRIOR entry. Stored as a flat 2100; the doubling for Royal Guardsmen and
    top officers is prose.
  - RACE. The book gives a distribution (85% Lemurian, 8% Meran, 6%
    Ichthylean, 1% other), not a closed list, so no race restriction is stored.
