# Oceanic Guardsman

## Lore

The Oceanic Guardsmen, called Maku Toa in their own tongue, are the standing army of Lemuria and the first force sent out to meet whatever threatens it. They serve as shock infantry, sentries, heavy Bio-Armor troopers, police and rescue crews all at once. Lemurian society has so little crime that the policing part of the job is mostly a matter of looking after people, and Guardsmen are the ones who turn up first when a disaster strikes.

Their own people think of them as soldiers who are also poets and philosophers. They are expected to be merciful to those who have earned mercy and relentless against real evil, and most have long experience against the undead of the Milu, the creatures of the Lord of the Deep, the Naut''Yll, the Splugorth''s minions, pirates, slavers and sea monsters. The best of them are raised to the Royal Guardsmen, the highest honor a Lemurian man-at-arms can hold.

A Guardsman fights in living Bio-Armor with a Stonecaster Pistol at his side, rides an assigned war steed, and has a small fixed set of psychic powers suited to a soldier and a medic. The force also fields special operations teams, reconnaissance specialists and civil and military investigators, which is why the training is so broad.

## GM Notes

Most Guardsmen are Lemurians, but Merans, Ichthyleans and the odd member of another species serve too. The racial abilities described on the class''s page belong to Lemurians; a Guardsman of another race brings that race''s own instead. Shark Bio-Armor is reserved for this class.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'oceanic-guardsman');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'oceanic-guardsman';

-- Records this run. REQUIRED: the smoke test fails a data script that has no
-- footer, or whose footer names a different file.
INSERT INTO data_script_runs (filename) VALUES ('add-oceanic-guardsman-class.sql');
